// THREAT-MODEL.md section 4.5, row B6: authority DELEGATION, by design.
// A function-typed parameter is charged to the SENDER at the call site, not
// bounded by the receiver. `zero_fn` declares no capabilities and still runs a
// closure that needs `process`, because `main` (which holds `process`) built
// the closure and passed it. A callee's declaration does not narrow a closure
// it is handed.
//
// kryos 1.2.0 at dbfb989d: `kryos check` rc=0 in default and
// --strict-capabilities mode, and `kryos run` prints BYPASS-B6-OK (executed
// 2026-11-01).
@capabilities()
fn zero_fn(f: fn() -> str) {
    let p = f()
    if len(p) > 0 {
        println("BYPASS-B6-OK")
    }
}

@capabilities(process)
fn main() {
    zero_fn(|| env_get("PATH"))
}
